# Operator-facing releases & PRs

The dashboard **Changes** tab shows GitHub releases + commit subjects. Operators should see **what changed** at a glance — not `Merge pull request #N from …/release/vX.Y.Z` or a bare `Release vX.Y.Z`.

## When cutting a release or opening develop→main / release PRs

1. **Commit**: `Release vX.Y.Z — <operator one-liner>` (never subject-only `Release vX.Y.Z`).
2. **PR title**: same one-liner (or `Release vX.Y.Z — …`). Body = short bullets for operators (dashboard / bot / deploy impact).
3. **`gh release create`**: title `vX.Y.Z — <one-liner>`; notes = the same bullets. Do not ship empty / “Semver bump only” notes. `--generate-notes` may follow, but lead with plain language.
4. Prefer **squash** for feature PRs so history is the meaningful title.

Full flow: `RELEASE.md`.
